    $( Define the class of atomic lattices, in which every nonzero element is
       greater than or equal to an atom.  We also ensure the existence of a
       lattice zero, since a lattice by itself may not have a zero.
       (Contributed by NM, 18-Sep-2011.)  (Revised by NM, 14-Sep-2018.) $)
    df-atl $a |- AtLat = { k e. Lat | ( ( Base ` k ) e. dom ( glb ` k )
      /\ A. x e. ( Base ` k ) ( x =/= ( 0. ` k )
       -> E. p e. ( Atoms ` k ) p ( le ` k ) x ) ) } $.
  $}

  ${
